From 325c97a1e7fef97c090c023ad7d18507f4252430 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Kennedy <nick@nick-kennedy.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:55:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: centre fdm_rate maps on a gaze point

With fdm_rate, rate maps can follow gaze. kk_fdm_set_gaze, exported for
the OpenXR layer in the same process, takes a point per view relative to
the render area; KK_FDM_GAZE simulates one ("x,y" or "sweep[:seconds]").
Gaze is latched at queue submission at most every 10 ms, so the passes
of a frame share one map. The column and row rate profiles taken from
the application's density map are shifted per view so that the middle
of their highest-rate band lands on the gaze point.

Rate map parameter blocks are recycled through a ring of eight per
density image instead of being kept until the image is destroyed, and
published copies are tracked by a map serial. Stitched chains whose
segments were recorded with different maps are re-recorded without
stitching under one latched gaze.

KK_DUMP_PASSES_DIR writes colour attachment 0 of multiview passes for
checking the final image.

AI-written commit text (biblioklept).

